<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The statistics of the datasets used in the experiments are presented. Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix A Statistics of the datasets ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the statistics for FrameNet, and Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix A Statistics of the datasets ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the statistics for Japanese FrameNet.
<span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
The average proportion of polysemous verbs in the test sets, which can evoke different frames depending on the context, was 30.3% for FrameNet and 19.1% for Japanese FrameNet.
</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Clustering Setting</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yamada et al. (2021)</a></cite>, we determine all clustering thresholds on the development set.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">One-step clustering</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ group-average agglomerative clustering and iteratively merge clusters until their total number equals the number of frames in the development set. We then set the threshold to the minimum inter-cluster distance observed at this final merge.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two-step clustering</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by applying X-Means clustering to each group of examples sharing the same frame-evoking word, automatically inferring the optimal cluster count while capping the maximum clusters <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> to the highest number of unique frames per verb in the development set.
We then perform group-average agglomerative merging on the resulting clusters until the proportion of same-lemma examples assigned to the same cluster matches the proportion recorded on the development set. The minimum inter-cluster distance at this matching merge point serves as the second-stage threshold.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Evaluation on Smaller Models</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the frame induction performance of our proposed method when applied to smaller variants of the models used in Sections 4 and 5: Gemma 3-1B<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-1b-it" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-1b-it</a></span></span></span>, Gemma 3-4B<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-4b-it" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-4b-it</a></span></span></span>, Llama 3.2-1B<span id="footnote11" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">11</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B</a></span></span></span>, and Llama 3.2-3B<span id="footnote12" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">12</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B</a>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div></span></span></span>.
Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix C Evaluation on Smaller Models ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the results on FrameNet, and Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix C Evaluation on Smaller Models ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the results on Japanese FrameNet.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" colspan="10"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:9.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span><span id="A3.T6.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Model</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" rowspan="2"><span id="A3.T6.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Size</span></td>
