<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Training time required for the DML experiments.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In deep metric learning, LoRA weights were applied to all linear layers.
Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix D Training Cost ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows the total and trainable parameters for each model after adding the LoRA layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The training was conducted on a single A100 GPU with 80GB VRAM, and the time required is shown in Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix D Training Cost ‣ FrameEOL:Semantic Frame Induction using Causal Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
For English FrameNet, an average of 27,537 instances were used for training; with a batch size of 32 over 20 epochs, the average number of training steps was 17,210.
For Japanese FrameNet, an average of 1,043 instances were used for training; with a batch size of 32 over 20 epochs, the average number of training steps was 652.</p>
</div>
</section>
